<!-- IPC v1.x: Keepalive (firmware 5.3.1)
     Observed on LPR-IP4 firmware 5.3.1 with HTTP POST V1. The body has no
     XML declaration. It is a config version 1.7 document with
     messageType keepalive and a deviceInfo block. No alarm data, no images.
     The camera reused one persistent HTTP connection for these posts.

     How often it arrives is set by the keep-alive interval in the camera's
     HTTP POST settings (keepaliveTimeval). With that setting at 90 s, the
     camera sent one every 90 s. 90 s is an example setting, not a fixed value.

     Older firmware uses a DeviceInfo root instead: see
     keepalive-older-firmware.xml. All values are placeholders. -->
<config version="1.7" xmlns="http://www.ipc.com/ver10">
<messageType>keepalive</messageType>
<deviceInfo>
<deviceName><![CDATA[LPR Camera]]></deviceName>
<ip><![CDATA[192.0.2.100]]></ip>
<mac><![CDATA[00:00:00:00:00:00]]></mac>
</deviceInfo>
</config>
